{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `r`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The protected observation `r` is a top-level data variable and is observed exactly once with a plain built-in sampling statement, `r ~ binomial_logit(n, b);`. Context data `N` and `n` are not scored. Each parameter has exactly one built-in prior before later use in the model block.
","model_safe_stan":"// http://openbugs.net/Examples/Surgical.html
// random effects model
// Stanified: use sigma instead of squared, move p to generated quantitites
// Narrower priors on mu and sigma
data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] int r;
  array[N] int n;
}
parameters {
  real mu;
  array[N] real b;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  mu ~ normal(0.0, 20);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 1); // remove sigma-squared
  b ~ normal(mu, sigma);
  r ~ binomial_logit(n, b);
}
generated quantities {
  array[N] real<lower=0, upper=1> p;
  array[N] real<lower=0> ranks;
  real pop_mean;
  pop_mean = inv_logit(mu);
  for (i in 1 : N) {
    p[i] = inv_logit(b[i]);
    ranks[i] = rank(b, i);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":4,"n":[6,5,6,6],"r":[3,3,2,6]}","protected_variables":["r"]}
